        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5aa62253-c41c-5c71-9f8f-2f2f2931335b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Laws: Lei Áurea\n- People: Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil; Dom Pedro II\n- Roles: Princess Imperial of Brazil; regent; heiress presumptive\n- Places: Brazil; Europe\n\nFacts:\n- Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, was born on 29 July 1846 and died on 14 November 1921.\n- Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, was the heiress presumptive to the throne of the Empire of Brazil and held the title Princess Imperial.\n- Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, was nicknamed \"the Redemptress.\"\n- On 13 May 1888, the Lei Áurea was adopted in Brazil as the law that abolished slavery.\n- On 13 May 1888, Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, signed the Lei Áurea while acting as regent for Emperor Dom Pedro II.\n- Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, opposed slavery, and Dom Pedro II was in Europe when she signed the Lei Áurea.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d0ef58cf-127e-541a-8bad-852f9a477433",
        "text": "Page: Lei Áurea. Sentence: The Lei Áurea (] ; English: Golden Law ), adopted on May 13, 1888, was the law that abolished slavery in Brazil.\nPage: Lei Áurea. Sentence: It was signed by Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil (1846–1921), an opponent of slavery, who acted as regent to Emperor Dom Pedro II, who was in Europe.\nPage: Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil. Sentence: Dona Isabel (English: Isabella; 29 July 1846 – 14 November 1921), nicknamed \"the Redemptress\", was the heiress presumptive to the throne of the Empire of Brazil, bearing the title of Princess Imperial.",
